<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 18.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 18.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Monday announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption in the period March 16-18.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 16 (actual) 202 bcm, 47 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 17 (forecast) 218 mcm, 51 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 18 (forecast) 242 mcm, 57 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 16 (actual) 10.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.4 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 17 (forecast) 10.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.5 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 18 (forecast) 8.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.6 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption to supply on Monday, with none expected on Tuesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
